:{"id":"EP4613300E","nombre":"Ayuntamiento de Gandía"},"hash":"510c5885601c54f2","ia":{"es":"Qué muestran los datos: Entre 2023 y 2025, este organismo adjudicó 54 contratos menores de servicios y suministros de más de 14.000 y hasta 15.000 euros, justo por debajo del límite legal. Si esos importes se repartieran como en la franja inmediatamente inferior, lo esperable serían 12,0 contratos. La razón entre observados y esperados es 4,5, con un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 3,1 a 6,6. En diciembre se adjudicó el 20 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 14 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 43 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.650 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no implica irregularidades. Puede deberse a factores como precios de mercado o necesidades específicas. No refleja actos maliciosos ni errores en la adjudicación.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden necesidades similares. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros ámbitos. Analizar si los contratos al límite coinciden con presupuestos cerrados o cambios en las demandas.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 54 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 12.0 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.5, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.1 to 6.6. December accounts for 20% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 14% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 5. Contract [1], for 14,650 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar patterns can occur due to seasonal demand or budget cycles. The number of contracts near the limit does not prove violations, as market prices or budget constraints may influence decisions.\nWhat can be checked: Check the contracts awarded in December for consistency with other contracts in the same category. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same service or supply. Verify if multiple contracts address the same need to assess if they were necessary or if they overlap.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["pFzRL9nPu6mHCIsjvJ3rhQ%3D%3D","vwt0Gzm1Ey07%2B9FIQYNjeQ%3D%3D","3gpP5PLPABJxseVhcqrkhw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}